course: dictionary
lesson: 14122
title: Finding the midpoint
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The midpoint is the point exactly in the middle, halfway between two ends. You can find it in a line, in a race, in a school term, or between two numbers. «The midpoint of the race was marked by a red flag.» The clue is the word halfway: the midpoint is the middle.
explain: In maths, the midpoint between two numbers is their average. Add the two numbers and divide by 2. «Find the midpoint between 4 and 10.» Add them: 4 + 10 = 14. Halve it: 14 ÷ 2 = 7. So the midpoint is 7, which is exactly halfway between 4 and 10.
explain: On a grid, you find the midpoint of two points by working out the middle of the x numbers and the middle of the y numbers. «The midpoint of (2, 4) and (6, 8) is (4, 6).» Check it: 2 and 6 average to 4, and 4 and 8 average to 6.
fact: The midpoint is the point exactly halfway between two ends.
fact: «Midpoint» can also mean the middle of a time, a journey or an event, as in «at the midpoint of the term».
fact: To find the midpoint of two numbers, add them and divide by 2.
fact: The midpoint between 4 and 10 is 7, because 7 is exactly halfway.
fact: On a grid, find the middle of the x numbers and the middle of the y numbers to find the midpoint of two points.
exercise: «Find the midpoint between 4 and 10.» What is the midpoint? | 6 | 8 | *7 | 14
exercise: «We reached the midpoint of the race at noon.» What does midpoint mean here? | *The middle of the race | The start line | A prize for the winner | The end of the race
exercise: What is the midpoint of (2, 4) and (6, 8)? | (2, 8) | (8, 12) | *(4, 6) | (3, 5)
test: «The midpoint of a line is exactly halfway along it.» What does midpoint mean? | *The point exactly in the middle of the line | A point at the very top | The point where the line ends | The longest point on the line
test: «The midpoint between 2 and 12 is what number?» | *7 | 14 | 10 | 5
exam: «At the midpoint of the term, Sam had read six books.» What is the midpoint of the term? | A school holiday | The last day of term | *Halfway through the term | The first day of term
